Rokk

Rokk is based on Terax (https://github.com/crynta/Terax-AI), licensed under
the Apache License, Version 2.0. The full license text is in LICENSE.

Changes made to the original Terax files are listed in docs/rokk/CHANGES.md.

The Rokk wordmark is drawn from the Cherry Bomb One font, used under the SIL
Open Font License, Version 1.1. The license text is in
docs/rokk/brand/CherryBombOne-OFL.txt.

The interface font is Geist Sans by Vercel, in collaboration with
basement.studio, used under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1. The
license text is in public/fonts/geist/OFL.txt.

Screen recording on macOS uses the screencapturekit crate
(https://github.com/doom-fish/screencapturekit-rs) and its dependencies
apple-cf, apple-metal and doom-fish-utils from the same doom-fish project, dual licensed
under the MIT License or the Apache License, Version 2.0. Rokk uses them under
the MIT License; the text is in docs/rokk/licenses/screencapturekit-LICENSE-MIT.txt.

Saving a zoomed copy of a recording on macOS uses the objc2-av-foundation and
objc2-core-media crates (https://github.com/madsmtm/objc2), licensed under the
zlib License, the Apache License, Version 2.0, or the MIT License. Rokk uses
them under the MIT License; the text is in docs/rokk/licenses/objc2-LICENSE-MIT.txt.
